    <p style="font-size:16px;">During a long drought, Mzee Lekishon watched his neighbours walk their cattle many kilometres in search of grass, and some animals died on the way. His own cows stayed healthy — because during the rains he had cut, dried and stored hay in a shed behind his house.</p>
