    <div style="background:#10233d;padding:20px;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:20px;border:1px solid #33415c;border-left:4px solid #22d3ee;">
    <h3 style="color:#c8e6c9;margin-top:0;">🔭 Business Background</h3>
    <p><strong>Layout principles:</strong> put the rabbit hutch on stilts at the edge of the pond so droppings fall in; put vegetable beds close to the pond for easy watering; put the poultry house near the compost heap and the vegetable garden; keep paths for easy work; plant a live fence of fodder shrubs around the plot; leave the pond in a sunny place for algae to grow. <strong>Design steps:</strong> list the components; decide their positions; sketch the plot to a simple scale on paper; label each unit; draw arrows to show flows of manure, water and feed; write a short key. <strong>Choosing model materials:</strong> reuse locally available waste materials such as wood offcuts, cartons, cardboard, paper, bottle tops, plastic lids, sticks, clay and dry grass — this also reduces waste. <strong>Scale:</strong> for example, 1 cm on the model can represent 1 m on the farm.</p>
    </div>
